# Transition state for K + H2O2 (2 waters, Grotthuss relay) -> KP
# (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8 item 1). See ../rc/job.inp for the full identification
# note (confirmed by direct connectivity analysis 2026-09-09) and the
# solvation/resource corrections applied here; both files carry the same
# fixes for the same reasons, not repeated in full below.
#
# The relay this TS captures (RC -> TS bond-length evidence, all four
# centres moving at once):
#   H2O2's own proton (H135) transfers to water 2 (O134)
#   water 2's own proton (H133) transfers to water 1 (O132)
#   water 1's own proton (H131) transfers to the ketone oxygen (O130)
#   H2O2's now-deprotonated oxygen (O136) simultaneously attacks the ketone
#     carbon (C129), forming the new C-O bond
# -- a four-centre concerted Grotthuss relay, not a bare HOO- addition and
# not a hydroxide-expulsion step. See conversation record 2026-09-09 for the
# full RC/TS bond-length table.
#
# Corrections from the orca_stuff version, 2026-09-09:
# 1. ALPB(Water) -> ddCOSMO(Water): so the QM1 (r2SCAN-3c) region -- where this
#    entire four-centre relay lives -- is actually solvated, not just the
#    QM2/xtb scaffold. See ../rc/job.inp for the manual citation.
# 2. Added Recalc_Hess 10: this project's first three attempts at a
#    different TS in this same QM/XTB style (K+peroxide+BnOH_bridged_
#    UNIDENTIFIED/, before its geometry was found to be misidentified)
#    plateaued for 40+ cycles on a single initial Hessian, and a second
#    attempt seeded from the drifted geometry then had 60% of its
#    displacement gradients fail outright. Recalc_Hess 10 (ORCA 6.1 manual,
#    "4.3. Transition State Searches": recommended when "the PES near the
#    TS can be very far from ideal for a Newton-Raphson step") refreshes the
#    exact Hessian periodically rather than trusting one RFO-updated
#    approximation for the whole search. Cheap here: each displacement
#    gradient on this QM region runs ~1.5 s, so a full recompute is on the
#    order of a couple of minutes at nprocs 8.
# 3. nprocs 12 / maxcore 2200 -> nprocs 8 / maxcore 4000: homelab-benchmarked
#    (COMPUTATIONAL.md Conventions, 2026-09-09).
#
# QM region unchanged from the version that already produced a QMRegion.xyz
# cleanly (no boundary/link-atom problem here). Geometry (job.xyz) is a warm
# start from that same prior run's converged ALPB-level TS
# (alpb_uncorrected/job_converged_alpb.xyz) rather than a fresh scan guess --
# solvation mainly changes electronics/energetics, not gross geometry, so
# this should already be close to the ddCOSMO-level TS. alpb_uncorrected/
# also holds an abandoned SMD-solvation attempt (sp_abandoned_smd_attempt/)
# from before this correction; plain CPCM/SMD are both rejected outright by
# ORCA for QM/XTB (see ../rc/job.inp) -- ddCOSMO was chosen because the
# manual is explicit it gets the same C-PCM/B-style propagation to QM1.

! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{128 129 130 131 138 132 133 139 134 135 136 137}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
Recalc_Hess 10
END

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
